# Testing Guidelines

## Test Framework
- Use Bun as the test runner
- Use `@testing-library/react` for component testing
- Use `@testing-library/jest-dom` for DOM matchers
- Use `happy-dom` for DOM environment

## Test Organization
- Place tests in `__tests__/` directories
- Use `.test.ts` or `.test.tsx` file extensions
- Group related tests in the same directory as source files
- Use descriptive test names

## Test Structure
```typescript
import { describe, it, expect, beforeEach } from 'bun:test';
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
import { Component } from './component';

describe('Component', () => {
  beforeEach(() => {
    // Setup
  });

  it('should render correctly', () => {
    render(<Component />);
    expect(screen.getByText('Expected text')).toBeInTheDocument();
  });
});
```

## Testing Patterns
- Test user interactions, not implementation details
- Use proper queries (getByRole, getByLabelText, etc.)
- Mock external dependencies
- Test error states and edge cases
- Use proper cleanup in tests

## Coverage
- Aim for high test coverage
- Focus on critical business logic
- Test user-facing functionality
- Use `bun test --coverage` for coverage reports

## Mocking
- Mock external APIs and services
- Use proper mock implementations
- Reset mocks between tests
- Mock at the appropriate level

## Test Data
- Use realistic test data
- Create reusable test fixtures
- Use factories for complex objects
- Keep test data minimal but complete